id: pm-gantt-chart-post-release-changelog
title: Keep release changelogs stable after tagging an empty pending window
description: Reproduce pre-tag versus post-tag drift with real SDK trackers; omit only the empty Unreleased placeholder while retaining historical releases and legitimate pending work.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-gantt-chart#214","gh:unbraind/pm-gantt-chart#215"
created_at: "2026-11-06T14:13:18.221Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T01:12:07.072Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T14:14:04.326Z",codex-sol,"Main 58a3ceb still fails npm run changelog:check with only an empty Unreleased section added. The pinned generator applies include-empty to every release window, including the synthetic post-tag pending window. Plan: preserve upstream generation, attribution, date and lint checks; omit only its exact empty Unreleased placeholder through one shared project entrypoint used by writes, checks and release notes. Add real SDK tracker fixtures for pre/post-tag identity, historical attribution, nonempty pending work, stale-output rejection and no-git diagnostics."
  "2026-11-06T14:16:50.431Z",codex-sol,"Failing-test-first proof: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/project-changelog.test.ts fails the matching-tag check with exactly the reported empty Unreleased diff; nonempty pending attribution and no-git refusal controls pass on main. The refined regression cases each also assert empty-window omission so behavioral reversion must fail both."
  "2026-11-06T14:23:49.986Z",codex-sol,"Verification: linked node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/project-changelog.test.ts test/compatibility-floor.test.ts passed 10/10 with zero skipped. Real SDK trackers cover pre/post matching tag byte identity, empty historical releases, legitimate pending work, historical attribution, prepend, release notes and step summary, stale-output rejection without writes, and no-git refusal. Behavioral revert proof in a disposable copy: replacing only omitEmptyUnreleased with return markdown fails both regression tests (0 passed, 2 failed); the fixed checkout passes. Lint, typecheck, build:test, duplication (0 percent), docstrings (132 declarations), release workflow and release date verifiers passed. Dependencies and thresholds remain pinned. CI will run the unchanged complete npm/Bun release gates on Node 22.18.0 and 26; the PR will enter the required queued bot-review loop immediately after opening. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-06T14:25:04.371Z",codex-sol,"CI topology clarification: Node 22.18.0 runs the constituent build, coverage, acceptance and changelog gates; Node 26 additionally runs the complete npm run release:check and bun run release:check commands. The final compatibility assertion also passed 8/8 after binding every package script to the shared rendering entrypoint."
  "2026-11-06T14:28:36.031Z",codex-sol,"Final fixture revision executes unchanged package scripts through temporary directory links. Linked tests passed 10/10 again with zero skipped; the behavioral revert still fails both tests (0/2 passed). Final lint and build:test passed. Strict health passes with a clean HOME and global Git configuration disabled; the normal HOME has a pre-existing globally discovered pm-github extension resolving PM CLI 2026.11.5 while this repo pins 2026.11.4. No dependency, global setup, provenance history, or telemetry configuration was changed. The existing historical-provenance warning is advisory. Claim remains released for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-06T17:42:47.165Z",codex-sol,"Resumed PR 215 after CodeRabbit review on 0aa9b00. Confirmed thread PRRT_kwDOSYpIas60m9ER: failed check returns before the requested step summary is appended, unlike the pinned generator. Add a failing real SDK tracker regression for stale, missing and current changelogs, retain failure status and read-only check behavior, and append the normalized summary on the failing branch. Existing issue 214 behavior and thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-06T17:43:30.389Z",codex-sol,"Failing-test-first proof for the review finding: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"checked drift\" test/project-changelog.test.ts failed (0 passed, 1 failed) because the summary file was absent after a stale check returned 1. The fix appends the same normalized Markdown on the failed-check branch before returning, preserving existing success and non-summary behavior."
  "2026-11-06T17:45:53.509Z",codex-sol,"Review fix focused test passed 1/1 with zero skipped. It confirms stale and missing checks return 1 without modifying or creating the changelog, append normalized output to the step summary once, and successful checks append once while callers without the flag create no summary. Behavioral revert in a disposable copy restored only the prior projectChangelog function and failed this test (0 passed, 1 failed) with the absent-summary assertion. Fixed source passes. Lint, typecheck, build:test, duplication (0 percent), and docstrings (132 declarations) passed. Existing linked test command includes the new case and is being rerun before the fix push."
  "2026-11-06T17:48:56.576Z",codex-sol,"Final review-fix verification: linked node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/project-changelog.test.ts test/compatibility-floor.test.ts passed 11/11, zero failures and zero skips. The focused checked-drift test passed 1/1 and failed 1/1 when only the summary fix was reverted in a disposable copy. Lint, typecheck, build:test, duplication and docstring gates passed. Push the code, documentation and this append-only tracker evidence together, answer and resolve the valid review thread after pushing, and immediately requeue CodeRabbit for the new head. Fresh CI will verify the full release gates."
  "2026-11-07T00:49:31.180Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR 215: fetched every review thread and all comments; exactly one unresolved finding PRRT_kwDOSYpIas60sBzA. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Remote head is current and contains main. Verified the wrapper ignores -o and uses the first --output instead of the pinned generator last-option precedence. Reuse the saved WIP regression only after checking its cases against the installed CLI; fix parsing, self-review the whole diff, prove behavioral reversion, and run targeted plus full npm/Bun release gates. No thread replies or resolutions are authorized in this round."
  "2026-11-07T00:51:59.449Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed saved WIP test fails on the remote implementation: output override regression 0 passed, 1 failed because -o did not select its destination. Fixed wrapper uses the pinned CLI exported parseArgs instead of a second output parser, covering both aliases, equals and split forms, mixed repeated options, flag-shaped filenames and flag-shaped title values. Self-review also found the summary-token filter stripped a forwarded --pm-arg value; preserve forwarded values and use parsed stdout/check/summary flags. Extended real SDK tracker tests cover successful strict checks, stale override refusal without writes, invalid missing/empty output values before writes, and forwarded-value refusal without a spurious summary."
  "2026-11-07T00:55:12.523Z",codex-agent,"Final behavioral revert proof in a disposable copy: restore only projectChangelog from the remote review head, retaining the new tests and all other fixed source. Exact command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"output overrides|forwarded pm arguments\" test/project-changelog.test.ts. Reverted: 0 passed, 2 failed, 0 skipped (missing selected output; forwarded summary token changed into stdout). Restoring the fixed function: 2 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped. Source checkout remained fixed throughout. Build and test typecheck, typecheck, lint, duplication (0 percent, 72 sources), docstrings (132 declarations), and strict tracker health passed; regenerated committed dist has no changes. The linked gate hit its default 120-second timeout under concurrent host load and is being retried with a 600-second cap. An inherited linked command required clone-local trust acknowledgement because this worktree branch differs from its recorded source branch; acknowledged the already-reviewed commands without modifying tracker provenance or policy."
  "2026-11-07T01:12:06.115Z",codex-agent,"Verification complete for review thread PRRT_kwDOSYpIas60sBzA and the related forwarded-value defect found in whole-PR self-review. Linked command node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/project-changelog.test.ts test/compatibility-floor.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts test/identity-audit.test.ts passed 25/25, zero failures or skips, on retry with a 600-second cap (103 seconds elapsed); the earlier default 120-second run timed out under host load. Full npm run release:check passed in 475 seconds and full bun run release:check passed in 473 seconds, each with 389/389 tests, zero failures or skips, 100 percent line/branch/function coverage across all 10 configured source files, and all 5 packed-package acceptance scenarios (npm/Bun local and global, plus minimum host). Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, zero-percent duplication, docstrings (132 declarations), brand, release-workflow, production audit, changelog/date and publish-attestation gates passed without changing thresholds or dependency pins. Committed dist rebuild is unchanged. Strict health passes with inherited provenance and telemetry advisory findings; no history repair or telemetry configuration changes. Behavioral revert and restoration counts are recorded above. Only the valid saved-WIP test was reused and extended. Finalize append-only tracker evidence and regenerate/check the changelog after releasing this claim; push this review fix, delete the saved local WIP branch, and leave all review threads untouched. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification; fresh pushed-head CI remains separate evidence."
